WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:21.100
[Music]

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:24.889
[Zoom in on sigh reading The Fourth Commandment: Native Food] 

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:31.260
[Narrator:] Thou shalt eat only the rations inspected, found fit and provided for thy use. 

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:38.280
For verily many native foods  contain poisons more treacherous than a Jap warlord.

00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:44.239
Somebody once said: the way to a man's heart is through his stomach. 

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.560
That is, everybody's but McGillicuddy's.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.180
He's particular! He doesn't like vienna sausage.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.140
He doesn't realize he's in the South Pacific.
He thinks he's in the Brown Derby!

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.259
[Daydreaming about turkey and steak]

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:03.489
[Looks like he's about to throw up and pushes
food away]

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:08.460
[Narrator:] Yeah, yeah, I know, Mac. It's monotonous. The same thing day-after-day.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.100
But it's good food and it's good for ya!

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:18.720
[McGillicuddy walks along the road, pausing to pull his belt tighter to a belthole that's labeled Damn Hungry]

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:23.210
[Narrator:] But Mac'll show 'em how to get along on a South Pacific island.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.880
He's a gourmet. A gastronomical Robinson Crusoe.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.909
[Looks up to see bananas]

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:35.909
[Narrator:] Yeah, they look like bananas, they peel like bananas, 

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.680
but they don't taste like bananas, do they?

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:44.710
You know why?  Because they're not bananas!

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:47.760
They're plantains and you can't eat 'em raw!

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.979
[Looks around and sees carrot-like plants]

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:54.189
[Narrator:] Well, what's this? A native victory garden no doubt.

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:57.799
Carrots? Rutabagas? Turnips?

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:00.909
Well, whatever they are, they're sure beauties.

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:03.469
[Sees natives taking care of garden]

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:09.080
[Narrator:] Well kept, well cultivated, but these boys are not just passing the time.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:12.420
They're passing the fertilizer, and from you-know-where.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.480
[Natives passing pots from head]

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:22.480
While this sort of fertilizer is very effective,
it produces a lot more than just vegetables.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.010
Take a look and you'll see what I mean.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.459
[Magnified view of carrot shows various germs wiggling and barking]

00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:29.399
[Mac drops carrots and wipes hands on clothes]

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.280
[Narrator:] Nauseating, ain't it?

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:40.880
[McGillicuddy starts walking again, along the way adjusting his belt to a hole that's labeled Starving!!]

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.420
[Narrator:] Oh boy, apples!

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:51.520
[Mac gobbles the apples right from the tree, but spits them out after seeing the sign 'Poison fruit']

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.980
[Narrator:] Yeah, Mac. Beach apples, good huh?

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.720
But you know what they do to ya? Well, the
juice contains an acid, which, uh, uh

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.320
attacks the tissue, and you have a chemical reaction,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.340
which results in a sort of a hot foot, uh, or rather a severe

00:03:08.349 --> 00:03:10.300
inflammation of the, uh...

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.460
Well anyway, it burns the hell out of your
tongue!

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:21.200
[Mac's tongue is on fire and he jumps into nearby water.]

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:30.840
[McGillicuddy sits at the base of a tree, Is reluctantly eating K Rations.]

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:35.560
That's the spririt, Mac! Eat your K Rations
and like it.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.740
[McGillicuddy, sneering:] Nyeeh!

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.920
[Smoke wafts over and Mac raises his head to sniff it.]

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.020
[Smoke spells out Eat at Dirty Joe's]

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.140
[Natives are sitting in a circle around a cooking fire.]

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:51.879
[Narrator:] Mac's brains are still in his stomach.

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:54.019
[He follows the smoke and eats with the natives.]

00:03:54.019 --> 00:03:56.040
[Narrator:] Well, the man who came to dinner.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.700
Look, Mac. We're not complaining about your manners, 

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.420
and it's all right to be friendly with the natives,

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.250
but their food is not prepared in the most
sanitary fashion.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:12.370
Very often, the food which they handle...what you're now packing away, is infested with

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:16.720
germs which are extremely difficult to digest.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.069
[Mac pats his bloated stomach in satisfaction, and hiccups.]

00:04:20.069 --> 00:04:22.159
[Narrator:] Oh, pardon me!

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.960
[Sign reads: Mess Special Today, Turkey]

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:34.540
[Mac waits in line outside the mess tent, smiling and waving.]

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:39.059
[Narrator:] Yeah, we see you, Mac! This is what you've been waiting for.

00:04:39.059 --> 00:04:45.259
Hey, Mac! In a couple of seconds, you'll have that big turkey dinner!

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:49.240
[Mac is seated in front of a large, steaming turkey on a plate.]

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:55.720
[Narrator:] Yum, yum! Roast turkey and cranberries! And...oh, here we go again.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.780
[Mac releases gas and runs to the head.]

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.200
[McGillicuddy:] CHARGE!

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:08.040
[Mac returns to find only turkey bones.]

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:14.789
[Narrator:] Too bad, Mac. Ya missed the boat, but they will have turkey again, sometime. 

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.240
But in the meantime ...

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.220
[A plate with sausage is placed in front of Mac, and the end of the sausage flaps open and neighs.]

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:27.400
[Music]

